A||||6||Sootah||What is the best way to remove water spots from paint? **Rehash**||||5||
Z||000000||Sootah||11-06-2001||01:38 AM||||Waterspots = Evil<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Waterspots.jpg"> <P>See that? How do I get that off without mashing the paint? I've got the glass cleaned up pretty good (not well enough, but I can't drive her yet so I don't care) but don't want to use CLR on the paint. Afraid of what that would do. I do have rubbing compound; Would that work?<P>I've also heard a few people mention 'claying' it or something to that effect. What is this?<P>Now most of the car isn't nearly that bad, I just took a pic of the worst of it to show you what I meant. Ah, yes, there are also water spots on my rims. How do I go about cleaning those?<P>And now just cause I want to show her off, (even if she's being an obstanant bìtch and not letting me 'ride' her) here she is. The <I>Black Beauty</I><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg"> <P><B>PEACE <I>-Sootah</B></I><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">     <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||5
Z||000001||RossT||11-06-2001||02:31 AM||||I would try clay.  I use claybar from <A HREF="http://www.zainobros.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zainobros.com</A>  .  It should remove it. Follow the instructions on how to use it.<P>you could also try a product called "goof-off" You can buy it at paint stores or hardware stores.  But you can not use it on <BR>plastic!!! only on painted metal. I have seen this stuff remove just about anything, but once again, keep it away from your plastic panels.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||11-06-2001||07:55 AM||||Mcguires has several products that may work. Body Scrub does wonders on painted surfaces. They have a cleaner product also.  Both products, to me, seem to be light duty polishing compounds that remove either deeply imbedded surface contaminents or just surface contaminents.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sootah||11-06-2001||08:24 AM||||So, think I should try the rubbing compound 1<sup>st</sup>? I wonder if a good old pressurewash would do it any good..?<P>Ah well, I'm off to work now. Bump<sup>1</sup>||||reg||5
Z||000004||Oreif||11-06-2001||08:47 AM||||First, Use Meguire's Body Scrub (to clean paint)<BR>Then, Meguire's Deep Crystal Polish (to polish)<BR>Finally, Meguires Deep Crystal Carnuba Wax (to protect)<P>Do this over the entire car. <BR>When done it should look close to this:<BR>(yes 2/3's is original paint on my car)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fcol_01_1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||6
